IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 12B -- Fee units (ss 48B and 48C).
-- Amounts are in dollars.

§ `Part 12B -- Fee units`

§§ `s 48B -- Value of fee unit`

-- src:978 | (1) A regulation may prescribe a monetary amount to be the value of a fee unit.
@ref s 48B(1) (src:978-978)
GIVEN `the amount is a monetary amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a regulation may prescribe the amount to be the value of a fee unit (s 48B(1))` IS
    IF `the amount is a monetary amount` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:979 | (2) The amount prescribed may include a fraction of a cent.
@ref s 48B(2) (src:979-979)
GIVEN `the amount includes a fraction of a cent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the amount prescribed may include a fraction of a cent (s 48B(2))` IS JUST TRUE

-- src:982 | (3) Without limiting the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, section 25, a regulation may prescribe different amounts for different Acts.
@ref s 48B(3) (src:982-982)
GIVEN `the amounts are prescribed for different Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a regulation may prescribe different amounts for different Acts (s 48B(3))` IS
    IF `the amounts are prescribed for different Acts` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- (4): the value of a fee unit for an Act is (a) the amount prescribed under this section; or (b) if no amount is prescribed -- $1.
-- src:983 | (4) The value of a fee unit for an Act is—
-- src:984 | (a) the amount prescribed under this section; or
-- src:985 | (b) if no amount is prescribed—$1.
@ref s 48B(4) (src:983-985)
GIVEN `the amount prescribed under this section for the Act, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the value of a fee unit for an Act (s 48B(4))` IS
    CONSIDER `the amount prescribed under this section for the Act, if any`
    WHEN JUST amount THEN amount
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 1

§§ `s 48C -- Working out amounts`

-- src:987 | (1) An Act may express a fee or other matter as a number (whether whole or fractional) of fee units.
@ref s 48C(1) (src:987-987)
GIVEN `the number of fee units is whole or fractional` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act may express a fee or other matter as a number of fee units (s 48C(1))` IS JUST TRUE

-- src:988 | (2) The Act may also provide for how an amount is to be rounded for the purpose of subsection (3).
@ref s 48C(2) (src:988-988)
GIVEN `the Act provides for how an amount is to be rounded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act may also provide for how an amount is to be rounded (s 48C(2))` IS JUST TRUE

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`x rounded to the nearest cent, rounding one-half upwards` MEANS (FLOOR (x * 100 + 0.5)) / 100

-- (3): the amount is the number of dollars obtained by (a) multiplying the value of a fee unit for the Act by the number of fee units; and
-- (b) rounding the result (i) in the way the Act provides, if it does; or (ii) otherwise to the nearest cent (rounding one-half upwards).
-- src:989 | (3) The amount of the fee or other matter is the number of dollars obtained by—
-- src:990 | (a) multiplying the value of a fee unit for the Act by the number of fee units; and
-- src:991 | (b) rounding the result—
-- src:992 | (i) if the Act provides for how the result is to be rounded—in that way; or
-- src:993 | (ii) otherwise—to the nearest cent (rounding one-half upwards).
@ref s 48C(3) (src:989-993)
GIVEN `the value of a fee unit for the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of fee units` IS A NUMBER
      `the result as rounded in the way the Act provides, if the Act provides for how the result is to be rounded` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount of the fee or other matter in dollars (s 48C(3))` IS
    CONSIDER `the result as rounded in the way the Act provides, if the Act provides for how the result is to be rounded`
    WHEN JUST rounded THEN rounded
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `x rounded to the nearest cent, rounding one-half upwards` (`the value of a fee unit for the Act` * `the number of fee units`)
